     start of each pivot row's own label cell opens a floating card with that
     row's thread; the key is the row's labels ([row field, value] pairs, sorted
     by field, as JSON), so it needs no key column. The REAL main.js booted
     through the REAL run path (stubbed query.php + manage_journal.php) on a
     27-row fixture: DEPT x FY x PI, AMOUNT. The report is saved as a PIVOT
     (state.pivot, per scenario below); the journal is on with row notes on and
     NO key column (the user's Option 1: the Row notes switch no longer needs
     one). ?scn=<name> picks the stored report; driver.js runs it.
     Spliced in by run.py from the index.php under test: the View Options
     journal panel (#journalRowConfig) at PV_VIEW_OPTIONS and the journal dialog
     (#journalLightbox) at PV_JOURNAL_LIGHTBOX. -->

